    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d639">

                <pb facs="0675" n="625" sameAs="frus:frus1894/pg625"/>

                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Taylor to Mr. Gresham.</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Legation of the United States</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Madrid</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1894-12-17"><hi rendition="#italic">December 17, 1894</hi></date>.
                        (Received December 28.)</dateline>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 272.]</seg></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: I have the honor to report that after the
                    receipt on Saturday morning of your telegram concerning the Cuban tariff on
                    flour and other American products, I at once arranged for a conference with the
                    minister of state for the afternoon of that day. Owing to a pressing engagement
                    at the time first fixed the minister postponed the interview until the afternoon
                    of yesterday, when I read to him your telegram, together with the text of
                    section 5 of the act of August 30, 1890, referred to therein. After a brief
                    conversation the minister assured me that he would at once refer the subject to
                    the minister of the colonies with an earnest recommendation that he do all in
                    his power to so arrange the Cuban tariff (a work now in progress) as to secure
                    to the <pb facs="0676" n="626" xml:id="pg626"/> United States the most favored
                    nation treatment. At the end of the interview I sent you a telegram. I shall
                    give this important subject my most careful consideration, and I will telegraph
                    any answer that may be received to your suggestion.</p>
                <p>I inclose herein, with translation, a copy of a personal note which I have just
                    received from the minister of state as to our interview above described.</p>
                <p>I am, etc.,</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Hannis Taylor.</hi></signed></closer>


                <xi:include href="d639-a1.xml" xpointer="d639-a1"/>
            </div>
